    <selectionEntry id="c10c-ff45-2494-5d51" name="Legion Saturnine Terminator Armour" publicationId="3970-79bb-bdc6-9599" page="91" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <profiles>
        <profile id="ffa0-fb95-a070-772d" name="Legion Saturnine Terminator Armour" hidden="false" typeId="b46c-270c-d29e-f0ff" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="0982-427b-1d4a-d07c">The technology for Exo-Armour was originally developed during Mankind's Dark Age of Technology. These sealed environment suits enabled maintenance crews of spacecraft to operate in extremely hazardous environments such as hard vacuum, the interior of plasma or fusion reactors, and in otherwise adverse atmospheric conditions. It was from here that the Mechanicum started their work, and in short order they had created working prototypes, the first suits of which were completed shortly before the beginning of the Great Crusade. By the end of the crusade, however, the inferno of war hungered for more materiel, and into such flames were suits old and new cast… Legion Saturnine Terminator Armour confers a 2+ Armour Save and a 4+ Invulnerable save, as well as the Hammer of Wrath (1) Special Rule. A unit that includes any models with Saturnine Terminator armour may not make Sweeping Advances. In addition, a model armed with Saturnine Terminator Armour is immune to the effects of both the Rad-Phage Special Rule and of the effects of Rad Grenades and Rad Furnace wargear.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry id="2bef-6f72-6f45-220a" name="Aspectum-Pattern Occularis Array" publicationId="3970-79bb-bdc6-9599" page="90" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <profiles>
        <profile id="c7f2-6b0a-cf9a-8834" name="Aspectum-Pattern Occularis Array" hidden="false" typeId="b46c-270c-d29e-f0ff" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="0982-427b-1d4a-d07c">A complex tangle of cogitators and auspex equipment slaved together, these powerful arrays can pierce darkness, circumvent terrain, and render cover useless. A model armed with this wargear has the Night Vision Special Rule, and any enemy model targeted by a Shooting Attack from this model suffers a -1 penalty to all Cover Saves it makes as a result of attacks made by this model.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry id="3bfb-a75f-d64a-f117" name="Ferromantic Deflector" publicationId="3970-79bb-bdc6-9599" page="11" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
